# Foreman metrics export

Generated 2026-10-20 · 5 runs counted · 2 stages run through Foreman

Both measures are defined as in `docs/metrics-baseline.md`: time to start ends at the spawn (CLI) or when the filled prompt is on the clipboard and the chat is open (chat); active time runs from the same start to the step done. Press Send is not part of either. Medians of an even count are the mean of the middle two; p95 is the nearest rank.

## Summary

| Measure | Surface | By hand (this file) | Foreman (Export metrics) |
|---|---|---|---|
| Steps logged | chat | 1 | 1 |
| Steps logged | CLI | 2 | 3 |
| Median seconds to start | chat | 45.0 | 8.4 |
| Median seconds to start | CLI | 110.3 | 5.2 |
| p95 seconds to start | chat | 45.0 | 8.4 |
| p95 seconds to start | CLI | 130.5 | 6.1 |
| Median active minutes per step | chat | 25.0 | 10.1 |
| Median active minutes per step | CLI | 23.8 | 15.1 |
| Manual edits per step | all | 1.00 | 0.50 |
| Mistakes per stage | all | 0.50 | — |

Foreman's manual edits are the proxies it can see: run-input interventions plus every Copy prompt on a CLI step. Foreman builds the command from the template, so it does not log mistakes; overrides applied are listed below.

## Kill check

| Surface | Baseline present | Median to start lower | Median active lower | Manual-edit proxies |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| chat | no (1 of 10 steps) | yes | yes | 0 |
| CLI | yes (2 steps) | yes | yes | 2 |

The check passes only when every row says yes and no step needed a manual prompt edit. Each proxy event needs an explanation in your Stage 9 attestation.

